   measured 1-sigma-ish budget (v02, quadrature): distance+gas+inclination = 13.8%;  adding IF + Upsilon treatment + class heterogeneity = 29.0%;  published: MLS16 20%, Desmond 2023 7.6% (sys)
   needed shift 13.0% = 1.01 x the distance+gas+inclination budget, 0.48 x the full budget, 0.65 x MLS16's quoted 20%
  [OK] B1 the shift needed to remove the tension is INSIDE the systematic budget (measured full budget and MLS16's 20%); the tension is not evidence against Omega_Lambda = 32 pi a0^2/(3 H0^2 c^2)
  [OK] B2 a single systematic (rescaling all SPARC distances by the H0 ratio) is by itself as large as the needed shift (>= 95% of it)
   The other side of the ledger: the same systematics, applied the other way, would push Omega_pred UP; and the IF choice alone spans Omega_pred = 0.59-0.98.  The 'prediction' Omega_Lambda inherits twice the fractional error of a0.

